<file path="INSTALLATION_GUIDE.md">
# NeoVids — manual de instalação, operação e validação

Este documento descreve uma instalação limpa em **Ubuntu 24.04 LTS** para o
ambiente local do NeoVids. O escopo é desenvolvimento/produção local em uma
única máquina: Docker Compose, cinco serviços, PostgreSQL/Redis internos,
Qwen3-TTS em uma GPU NVIDIA e LiteLLM externo.

O diretório recomendado é `/home/$USER/workspaces/neovids`. Não coloque o
workspace em `/mnt/c`, em um disco de gameplay ou em uma pasta sincronizada:
Docker, PostgreSQL e arquivos de mídia têm desempenho e permissões melhores no
filesystem Linux.

## 1. Requisitos e layout

Recomendado:

- Ubuntu 24.04 LTS 64-bit, atualizado;
- 8 GB de RAM é o mínimo operacional, 16 GB ou mais é preferível;
- GPU NVIDIA com VRAM suficiente para o modelo Qwen configurado (a máquina
  validada possui RTX 2060 12 GB);
- pelo menos 100 GB livres para imagens/cache, além do espaço dos vídeos;
- acesso à internet durante a instalação e o primeiro download dos modelos;
- credenciais válidas do LiteLLM para embeddings e alinhamento quando essas
  funções forem usadas.

Layout final:

```text
/home/SEU_USUARIO/workspaces/neovids/
├── ideas-hub/
├── media-indexer/
├── orchestrator/
├── qwen3-tts-workshop/
├── video-composer/
└── neovids-infra/          # CLI, overrides e documentação operacional
```

Dados persistentes ficam dentro dos repositórios (bind mounts) ou em volumes
Docker nomeados. **Nunca remova volumes para “reinstalar”.**

## 2. Ubuntu, Git e utilitários

Após instalar o Ubuntu:

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt full-upgrade -y
sudo apt install -y git curl ca-certificates gnupg jq unzip ffmpeg \
  build-essential python3 python3-venv python3-pip
sudo timedatectl set-timezone America/Sao_Paulo
mkdir -p ~/workspaces/neovids
```

`ffmpeg`/`ffprobe` são úteis para smoke tests locais; os containers também
contêm suas próprias ferramentas.

## 3. Driver NVIDIA e suporte Docker à GPU

Em uma máquina NVIDIA, instale o driver recomendado e reinicie:

```bash
ubuntu-drivers devices
sudo ubuntu-drivers autoinstall
sudo reboot
```

Valide depois do reboot:

```bash
nvidia-smi
```

Instale o toolkit NVIDIA para containers seguindo o repositório oficial:

```bash
curl -fsSL https://nvidia.github.io/libnvidia-container/gpgkey | \
  sudo gpg --dearmor -o /usr/share/keyrings/nvidia-container-toolkit-keyring.gpg
curl -s -L https://nvidia.github.io/libnvidia-container/stable/deb/nvidia-container-toolkit.list | \
  sed 's#^deb https://#deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/nvidia-container-toolkit-keyring.gpg] https://#g' | \
  sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/nvidia-container-toolkit.list
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y nvidia-container-toolkit
sudo nvidia-ctk runtime configure --runtime=docker
sudo systemctl restart docker
docker run --rm --gpus all nvidia/cuda:12.4.1-base-ubuntu24.04 nvidia-smi
```

Se o último comando falhar, pare aqui: Qwen não ficará operacional até o
driver/runtime serem corrigidos. Não altere `DEVICE`, `DTYPE` ou o modelo para
contornar uma instalação incompleta.

## 4. Docker Engine e Compose

Remova pacotes conflitantes e instale o Docker pelo repositório oficial:

```bash
for p in docker.io docker-doc docker-compose podman-docker containerd runc; do
  sudo apt remove -y "$p" 2>/dev/null || true
done
sudo install -m 0755 -d /etc/apt/keyrings
curl -fsSL https://download.docker.com/linux/ubuntu/gpg | \
  sudo gpg --dearmor -o /etc/apt/keyrings/docker.gpg
sudo chmod a+r /etc/apt/keyrings/docker.gpg
echo "deb [arch=$(dpkg --print-architecture) signed-by=/etc/apt/keyrings/docker.gpg] https://download.docker.com/linux/ubuntu $(. /etc/os-release && echo $VERSION_CODENAME) stable" | \
  sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/docker.list >/dev/null
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y docker-ce docker-ce-cli containerd.io docker-buildx-plugin docker-compose-plugin
sudo systemctl enable --now docker
sudo usermod -aG docker "$USER"
newgrp docker
docker version
docker compose version
```

Se o Ubuntu estiver sendo executado dentro de WSL2, mantenha Docker Desktop ou
Docker Engine configurado de forma consistente; não instale duas daemons
concorrentes. Para uma instalação Ubuntu nativa, o `systemctl` acima é o fluxo
esperado.

## 5. Clonagem dos repositórios

```bash
cd ~/workspaces/neovids
git clone git@github.com:bernardoadca18/ideas-hub.git
git clone git@github.com:bernardoadca18/media-indexer.git
git clone git@github.com:bernardoadca18/orchestrator.git
git clone git@github.com:bernardoadca18/qwen3-tts-workshop.git
git clone git@github.com:bernardoadca18/video-composer.git
git clone git@github.com:bernardoadca18/neovids-infra.git
```

Se SSH ainda não estiver configurado, use HTTPS temporariamente ou configure
uma chave GitHub. Não copie um `.env` de outra máquina sem revisar segredos.

Crie os caminhos de conveniência, que apontam para o repositório operacional:

```bash
cd ~/workspaces/neovids
ln -s neovids-infra/scripts scripts
ln -s neovids-infra/infra infra
```

## 6. Configuração dos serviços

Cada serviço possui `.env.example`. Copie-o para `.env` no respectivo
repositório e preencha somente os segredos/URLs necessários:

```bash
cd ~/workspaces/neovids
cp ideas-hub/.env.example ideas-hub/.env
cp media-indexer/.env.example media-indexer/.env
cp orchestrator/.env.example orchestrator/.env
cp qwen3-tts-workshop/.env.example qwen3-tts-workshop/.env
cp video-composer/.env.example video-composer/.env
cp neovids-infra/infra/.env.example neovids-infra/infra/.env
chmod 600 */.env
```

Valores operacionais importantes:

| Serviço | Porta | Observação |
|---|---:|---|
| Ideas Hub API/frontend | 8000/5173 | banco `ideas-hub-db-data` |
| Media Indexer API | 8012 | PostgreSQL 5435; storage local; Whisper lazy |
| Orchestrator API/frontend | 8011/5174 | PostgreSQL 5434; Redis 6380 |
| Qwen Voice | 8889 | GPU, jobs SQLite e outputs persistentes |
| Video Composer | 8013 | SQLite/outputs no volume nomeado |
| LiteLLM externo | 4000 | não é gerenciado pelo NeoVids |

No Media Indexer, configure `LITELLM_BASE_URL` alcançável pelo container e uma
`LITELLM_API_KEY` válida. No Qwen, preserve o `MODEL_REVISION` pinado, o
`DEFAULT_VOICE_PROFILE` e as referências em `data/references`. Não coloque
chaves em Git, logs ou imagens.

No arquivo operacional:

```bash
sed -i "s#^NEOVIDS_BACKUP_ROOT=.*#NEOVIDS_BACKUP_ROOT=$HOME/backups/neovids#" \
  neovids-infra/infra/.env
mkdir -p "$HOME/backups/neovids"
chmod 700 "$HOME/backups/neovids"
```

Os backups são criados apenas quando há migração pendente; uma inicialização
normal já no head não cria dump redundante.

## 7. Primeiro diagnóstico e inicialização

Execute sempre a partir da raiz:

```bash
cd ~/workspaces/neovids
./scripts/neovids doctor
```

Em uma instalação limpa o diagnóstico deve indicar `FRESH`. Faça a primeira
subida com rebuild explícito:

```bash
./scripts/neovids up --build
```

O CLI cria a rede externa `neovids`, os cinco volumes canônicos, aplica
migrations e inicia databases, APIs, workers e frontends em ordem. Acompanhe:

```bash
./scripts/neovids status
./scripts/neovids health
./scripts/neovids logs qwen
```

Depois da primeira instalação, `./scripts/neovids up` basta para iniciar
imagens já construídas. Use `--build` após mudanças de código, dependências ou
Dockerfiles.

## 8. Smoke mínimo obrigatório

```bash
curl --fail http://127.0.0.1:8000/health/ready
curl --fail http://127.0.0.1:8012/health/ready
curl --fail http://127.0.0.1:8011/health/ready
curl --fail http://127.0.0.1:8889/health/ready
curl --fail http://127.0.0.1:8013/health/ready
curl --fail http://127.0.0.1:4000/health/readiness   # externo, se configurado
```

Abra `http://localhost:5173` e `http://localhost:5174` para os frontends. O
`doctor`/`health` pode informar Ollama indisponível; isso é opcional. LiteLLM
é obrigatório apenas para os fluxos que geram embeddings/alinhamento.

Para um teste funcional controlado, use os scripts de smoke documentados nos
repositórios (ASR/visual/temporal/candidate/alignment e o smoke Stage 17 do
Orchestrator). Não use mídia de gameplay real antes de confirmar storage,
volumes e espaço em disco.

## 9. Operação diária e encerramento seguro

```bash
./scripts/neovids status
./scripts/neovids health
./scripts/neovids logs media-indexer
./scripts/neovids restart qwen
```

Para parar tudo sem apagar dados:

```bash
./scripts/neovids down
docker ps --format '{{.Names}}' | grep -E 'ideas|media|orchestrator|qwen|video' || true
docker volume ls --format '{{.Name}}' | grep -E 'ideas-hub|media-indexer|orchestrator|video-composer'
```

Nunca use `docker compose down -v`, `docker volume prune`, `docker system
prune` ou `rm -rf` nos diretórios de dados. O restart do Docker/Ubuntu não deve
ressuscitar serviços NeoVids depois de `down`.

## 10. Mídia, backups e capacidade

O Media Indexer guarda fontes/derivados em `media-indexer/storage`; o Qwen usa
`data/jobs`, `data/outputs` e `data/references`; o Orchestrator guarda áudio em
`data/audio`. Faça backup desses diretórios e dos volumes PostgreSQL conforme a
política do projeto antes de trocar disco/OS. Não monte a unidade de footage no
Compose: selecione fontes explicitamente pela API.

Monitore uma máquina com pouca RAM durante Qwen + Whisper + Composer:

```bash
free -h; swapon --show; nvidia-smi; docker stats --no-stream
df -h ~/workspaces/neovids
```

Evite executar geração Qwen, transcrição e renderização pesada concorrentes em
outras aplicações GPU. O worker Qwen é serial por desenho.

## 11. Validação de desenvolvimento

Após clonar ou atualizar um serviço, execute seus testes no diretório indicado:

```bash
cd ~/workspaces/neovids/media-indexer/backend
pytest
ruff check app tests
mypy app
alembic upgrade head

cd ~/workspaces/neovids/ideas-hub/backend && pytest
cd ~/workspaces/neovids/orchestrator/backend && pytest
cd ~/workspaces/neovids/qwen3-tts-workshop && pytest
cd ~/workspaces/neovids/video-composer && npm ci && npm test
```

Os testes normais usam providers fakes e não baixam Qwen/Whisper. Smokes de GPU,
LiteLLM, pgvector e mídia real são opt-in e devem ser reportados separadamente.

## 12. Troubleshooting

**`doctor` indica PARTIAL / AMBIGUOUS.** Não crie volumes substitutos. Verifique
o nome exato dos cinco volumes canônicos e restaure o volume ausente a partir do
backup.

**Readiness falha.** Rode `status`, depois `logs <service>`. Confirme portas,
permissões dos binds, espaço em disco e `docker info`. Não contorne migrations
ou edite linhas de banco manualmente.

**Qwen não fica pronto.** Valide `nvidia-smi`, `docker run --gpus all ...`,
referência WAV/TXT e o cache Hugging Face. O modelo é carregado no lifespan;
importar o código não o baixa.

**LiteLLM retorna 401/timeout.** Corrija a credencial/endpoint no ambiente
externo. Não remova autenticação nem substitua o provider; os testes locais
devem usar fakes.

**Pouca RAM/swap.** Pare jobs, mantenha apenas um worker GPU e aumente memória
física/swap do Ubuntu. Não altere precisão/modelo como primeira medida.

**Código alterado não aparece no container.** Use `./scripts/neovids up --build`.
O `up` sem `--build` deliberadamente não adivinha se uma imagem está obsoleta.

## 13. Atualizações e rollback operacional

```bash
cd ~/workspaces/neovids
for repo in ideas-hub media-indexer orchestrator qwen3-tts-workshop video-composer neovids-infra; do
  git -C "$repo" status --short
  git -C "$repo" pull --ff-only
done
./scripts/neovids doctor
./scripts/neovids up --build
./scripts/neovids health
```

Leia o changelog/diff antes de migrations. O CLI faz backup quando detecta
migração pendente; downgrade é uma operação deliberada e deve ser executada no
repositório do serviço, nunca apagando o volume.

## 14. Limites arquiteturais

Este ambiente é uma implantação local confiável, de uma réplica. TLS,
autenticação pública, rate limiting, múltiplos workers GPU, brokers e
orquestração Kubernetes não fazem parte desta instalação. Ideas Hub mantém a
intenção editorial; Media Indexer mantém evidências; Orchestrator coordena;
Qwen sintetiza; Video Composer renderiza. O próximo trabalho de produto é a
integração com o workflow `game_analysis`, não uma nova camada de
infraestrutura.

## Checklist de aceite

- [ ] Ubuntu 24.04 atualizado e timezone definido
- [ ] `nvidia-smi` e teste `docker --gpus all` funcionando
- [ ] Docker Engine, Buildx e Compose plugin instalados
- [ ] seis repositórios clonados e com `git status` compreensível
- [ ] `.env` criado sem segredos versionados
- [ ] `doctor` sem erro e instalação `FRESH`/`EXISTING` coerente
- [ ] `up --build`, migrations e todos os health checks OK
- [ ] Qwen `/health/ready` OK e referência carregada
- [ ] smoke funcional executado com fakes ou mídia curta controlada
- [ ] backups fora do Git e volumes preservados
- [ ] `down` deixa zero containers NeoVids ativos
</file>

<file path="infra/README.md">
# NeoVids local operations

The authoritative operational sources live in the dedicated `neovids-infra`
Git repository. Workspace-level `infra` and `scripts` paths are relative
symlinks retained only for operator convenience. The CLI resolves the workspace
from the repository location, so the repository can be moved together with its
five sibling service repositories without embedding an absolute host path.

This directory coordinates the five independent NeoVids Compose projects. It
does not replace their service-owned Compose files, move business logic, or own
LiteLLM/Ollama. The operational layer adds a shared API backplane and one safe
development lifecycle.

## Normal workflow

From `/home/bernardo/workspaces/neovids`:

```bash
./scripts/neovids doctor
./scripts/neovids up
./scripts/neovids status
./scripts/neovids health
./scripts/neovids logs media-indexer
./scripts/neovids down
```

`up` works from a cold image/cache state. It validates installation mode and
bind-mount identities, creates the external `neovids` network when absent,
starts only the three application databases and Orchestrator Redis, verifies
representative existing table contents, builds missing images, inspects Alembic
state, and starts APIs in dependency order. When at least one database has a
pending migration, it writes logical PostgreSQL backups outside Git/volumes
before upgrading. A normal current startup does not create another full dump.
Readiness polling is bounded; fixed sleeps are not used as the primary gate.

Use `./scripts/neovids up --build` after source or dependency changes that must
be copied into images. Plain `up` builds only missing images and intentionally
does not guess whether an existing image is stale. `./scripts/neovids build`
rebuilds all application images without starting the stack.

`down` executes project-scoped `docker compose down --remove-orphans` in reverse
dependency order. It never passes `-v`, never prunes, leaves the external
network in place, and never manages LiteLLM, Ollama, or unrelated containers.
Removing the application containers is deliberate: starting Docker or opening
WSL after `down` cannot resurrect Qwen, Whisper workers, rendering, or workflow
workers through a restart policy.

## Ownership and dependency graph

```text
LiteLLM / Ollama (external, detected only)

Ideas Hub ────────────────> Media Indexer
                                  ^
                                  |
Orchestrator ─> Ideas Hub         |
             ├> Qwen Voice        |
             ├> Media Indexer ----+
             └> Video Composer ---+
                         |
                         └> Orchestrator
```

Databases remain attached only to their service-local default networks. The
external `neovids` bridge attaches application APIs that communicate across
repositories. Stable aliases are:

| Alias | Container port | Owner |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| `ideas-hub` | 8000 | Ideas Hub backend |
| `media-indexer` | 8000 | Media Indexer API/worker |
| `qwen-voice` | 8889 | Qwen Voice Service |
| `video-composer` | 8013 | Video Composer |
| `orchestrator-api` | 8000 | Orchestrator API |

The Orchestrator/Composer bidirectional runtime relationship is not represented
as a circular Compose `depends_on`. Each side starts independently and reports
eventual readiness.

## Host port inventory

| Service | Host port | Readiness |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| Ideas Hub API | 8000 | `/health/ready` |
| Ideas Hub frontend | 5173 | HTTP root |
| Ideas Hub PostgreSQL | 5432 | `pg_isready` |
| Orchestrator API | 8011 | `/health/ready` |
| Orchestrator frontend | 5174 | HTTP root |
| Orchestrator PostgreSQL | 5434 | `pg_isready` |
| Orchestrator Redis | 6380 | `redis-cli ping` |
| Media Indexer API | 8012 | `/health/ready` |
| Media Indexer PostgreSQL | 5435 | `pg_isready` |
| Qwen Voice | 8889 | `/health/ready` |
| Video Composer | 8013 | `/health/ready` |
| LiteLLM (external) | 4000 | `/health/readiness` |
| Ollama (external, optional) | 11434 | `/api/tags` |

Liveness endpoints do not invoke models, embeddings, FFmpeg, Chromium, or jobs.
Orchestrator readiness checks its durable stores and the four required service
APIs. LiteLLM is checked separately because NeoVids does not own its lifecycle.

## Durable storage contract

The CLI refuses to start when an established named volume is absent:

| Store | Effective storage |
| --- | --- |
| Ideas Hub PostgreSQL | `ideas-hub-db-data` |
| Media Indexer PostgreSQL | `media-indexer_media-indexer-db-data` |
| Media Indexer model cache | `media-indexer_media-indexer-model-cache` |
| Orchestrator PostgreSQL | `orchestrator-db-data` |
| Video Composer data/SQLite/outputs | `video-composer_video-composer-data` |
| Media Indexer managed media | `media-indexer/storage` bind mount |
| Orchestrator narration | `orchestrator/data/audio` bind mount |
| Qwen model cache | `qwen3-tts-workshop/cache/huggingface` bind mount |
| Qwen references/jobs/outputs | `qwen3-tts-workshop/data/*` bind mounts |

Compose project names are explicit in the CLI so implicit Media Indexer and
Composer volume names cannot drift. Backups default to
`$HOME/backups/neovids/<UTC timestamp>` with mode-restricted files. Set
`NEOVIDS_BACKUP_ROOT` to another non-repository path if needed.

## Installation modes

The five canonical named volumes form one installation identity:

- **existing**: all five exist; startup verifies representative database
  content and reuses them;
- **fresh**: none exists; `up` creates exactly those canonical volumes and
  initializes schemas without making meaningless empty-database backups;
- **partial/ambiguous**: only some exist; startup fails closed before starting
  databases or creating replacements.

Fresh bootstrap creates only the known writable bind directories. Qwen's
version-controlled reference WAV/text must still be present, and service-local
`.env` configuration remains the operator's responsibility. Never remove real
volumes to test bootstrap behavior; the CLI's shell tests use a fake Docker
boundary.

Backups are never deleted automatically. Review `$NEOVIDS_BACKUP_ROOT`
periodically and move or remove obsolete timestamped sets only after an
operator confirms their retention requirements.

## Source changes and builds

| Service | Development source behavior | Rebuild for a durable image |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Ideas Hub backend | source is copied into the image | `up --build` or `build` |
| Ideas Hub frontend | `src` is bind-mounted in local Compose; dependencies are in the image | rebuild after dependency/Dockerfile changes |
| Media Indexer | source is copied into the image | `up --build` or `build` |
| Qwen Voice | runtime source/config are copied into the image; data/cache are mounted | `up --build` or `build` |
| Video Composer | source is copied into the image | `up --build` or `build` |
| Orchestrator backend/frontend | repository source is bind-mounted in local Compose | rebuild after dependency/Dockerfile changes |

Never use `docker compose down -v`, `docker volume prune`, `docker system
prune`, or broad host-wide cleanup as part of normal NeoVids operation. Safe
cleanup of old caches/outputs remains a deliberate, store-specific operator
action and is not implemented by this CLI.

## Disk and footage safety

No root command scans `W:\`, `/mnt/w`, other Windows drive roots, managed media,
model caches, or generated output trees. Media source selection remains an
explicit operator action. No footage drive is mounted by the orchestration
overrides. Docker build contexts exclude virtual environments, Node modules,
model caches, media storage, outputs, coverage, Git metadata, and local secrets.

## GPU and model lifecycle

Qwen is the canonical voice service. It loads one pinned model through FastAPI
lifespan, caches voice prompts, owns one bounded serial GPU worker, and receives
30 minutes for graceful shutdown. Media Indexer keeps Faster-Whisper lazy and
reuses one loaded model per process. Root orchestration controls when these
services run; it does not change model, revision, precision, sampling, ASR beam,
frame quality, render profile, or any Stage 1-18 production semantics.

On a constrained workstation, avoid running unrelated GPU workloads while Qwen
or Faster-Whisper is active. GPU scheduling and device/precision changes are
intentionally outside this hardening layer.

## Logs and subprocesses

Service Compose files use Docker's `local` driver with bounded rotation. Python
services run with Docker init enabled; Qwen and long-running workers have
explicit grace periods. Video Composer already embeds `tini` and waits for its
active worker during SIGTERM. These settings improve child reaping without
changing FFmpeg/Remotion output.

`./scripts/neovids logs` returns the latest 200 lines rather than following all
services indefinitely. Pass a service group to narrow output.

## Cold recovery and troubleshooting

1. Run `./scripts/neovids doctor`. Missing established volumes/bind mounts are
   fatal; an absent shared network is expected before the first `up`.
2. Check that the Docker daemon and NVIDIA runtime are available.
3. Run `./scripts/neovids up`. A missing required table stops startup before
   application migrations.
4. If readiness fails, inspect `./scripts/neovids status` and
   `./scripts/neovids logs <service>`.
5. LiteLLM/Ollama failures are reported but never repaired or replaced by this
   tooling. Fix them in their owning deployment.

An external container may be marked unhealthy because its own image lacks the
binary used by its Docker healthcheck even while its HTTP readiness endpoint is
healthy. The NeoVids CLI uses the HTTP contract as the external dependency
signal and reports the Docker discrepancy separately during diagnosis.

The service repositories remain independently operable with their original
Compose commands. Repository-local Compose no longer uses automatic restart;
an operator explicitly starts it and `docker compose down` remains non-
destructive to named volumes.

## Host-level settings

WSL systemd and Docker are host responsibilities. This layer does not edit
`/etc/wsl.conf`, `.wslconfig`, Docker Desktop settings, Windows startup,
Defender, Search indexing, or mounted-drive policy. Docker/containerd may start
with WSL, but after `neovids down` there are no NeoVids application containers
for the daemon to restart.

TLS, authentication, and public rate limiting remain deployment concerns. The
documented ports target a trusted local development network.
</file>

<file path="scripts/neovids">
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -Eeuo pipefail

SCRIPT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd -P)"
INFRA_REPO_DIR="$(cd "$SCRIPT_DIR/.." && pwd -P)"
ROOT_DIR="${NEOVIDS_WORKSPACE_ROOT:-$(cd "$INFRA_REPO_DIR/.." && pwd -P)}"
NETWORK_NAME="${NEOVIDS_NETWORK:-neovids}"
BACKUP_ROOT="${NEOVIDS_BACKUP_ROOT:-$HOME/backups/neovids}"

usage() {
  cat <<'EOF'
Usage: ./scripts/neovids <command> [service|option]

Commands:
  doctor                 Safe, read-only host and dependency diagnostics
  up [--build]           Start the stack; optionally rebuild all images first
  down                   Remove only NeoVids containers; preserve all data
  restart [service]      Restart the stack or one application group
  status [service]       Show Compose status
  health                 Check host endpoints and external dependencies
  logs [service]         Show the latest service logs
  build                  Build application images using existing lockfiles

Service groups: ideas-hub, media-indexer, qwen, video-composer, orchestrator
EOF
}

compose() {
  local group="$1"
  shift
  local repo project base override
  case "$group" in
    ideas-hub)
      repo="ideas-hub"
      project="ideas-hub"
      base="docker-compose.yml"
      override="ideas-hub.yml"
      ;;
    media-indexer)
      repo="media-indexer"
      project="media-indexer"
      base="docker-compose.yml"
      override="media-indexer.yml"
      ;;
    orchestrator)
      repo="orchestrator"
      project="orchestrator"
      base="docker-compose.yml"
      override="orchestrator.yml"
      ;;
    qwen)
      repo="qwen3-tts-workshop"
      project="qwen3-tts-workshop"
      base="docker-compose.yaml"
      override="qwen3-tts-workshop.yml"
      ;;
    video-composer)
      repo="video-composer"
      project="video-composer"
      base="docker-compose.yml"
      override="video-composer.yml"
      ;;
    *)
      printf 'Unknown service group: %s\n' "$group" >&2
      return 2
      ;;
  esac
  (
    cd "$ROOT_DIR/$repo"
    NEOVIDS_NETWORK="$NETWORK_NAME" docker compose \
      --project-name "$project" \
      --file "$base" \
      --file "$INFRA_REPO_DIR/infra/orchestration/$override" \
      "$@"
  )
}

require_command() {
  command -v "$1" >/dev/null 2>&1 || {
    printf 'Required command is unavailable: %s\n' "$1" >&2
    return 1
  }
}

require_docker() {
  require_command docker
  docker info >/dev/null 2>&1 || {
    printf 'Docker daemon is unavailable.\n' >&2
    return 1
  }
}

required_volumes() {
  printf '%s\n' \
    ideas-hub-db-data \
    media-indexer_media-indexer-db-data \
    media-indexer_media-indexer-model-cache \
    orchestrator-db-data \
    video-composer_video-composer-data
}

verify_volume_identity() {
  local missing=0 volume
  while IFS= read -r volume; do
    if docker volume inspect "$volume" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
      printf 'volume %-52s OK\n' "$volume"
    else
      printf 'volume %-52s MISSING\n' "$volume" >&2
      missing=1
    fi
  done < <(required_volumes)
  if ((missing)); then
    printf 'Refusing startup: an established durable volume is missing.\n' >&2
    return 1
  fi
}

detect_installation_mode() {
  local present=0 total=0 volume
  while IFS= read -r volume; do
    total=$((total + 1))
    if docker volume inspect "$volume" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
      present=$((present + 1))
    fi
  done < <(required_volumes)

  if ((present == total)); then
    INSTALLATION_MODE="existing"
  elif ((present == 0)); then
    INSTALLATION_MODE="fresh"
  else
    INSTALLATION_MODE="partial"
  fi
}

prepare_installation() {
  detect_installation_mode
  case "$INSTALLATION_MODE" in
    existing)
      printf 'installation %-47s EXISTING\n' "NeoVids durable state"
      verify_volume_identity
      verify_bind_mounts
      ;;
    fresh)
      printf 'installation %-47s FRESH\n' "NeoVids durable state"
      printf 'Compose will create the five canonical named volumes.\n'
      initialize_fresh_bind_mounts
      ;;
    partial)
      printf 'installation %-47s PARTIAL / AMBIGUOUS\n' "NeoVids durable state" >&2
      verify_volume_identity || true
      printf 'Refusing startup: restore the missing established volumes or remove ambiguity manually.\n' >&2
      return 1
      ;;
  esac
}

initialize_fresh_bind_mounts() {
  local paths=(
    "$ROOT_DIR/media-indexer/storage"
    "$ROOT_DIR/orchestrator/data/audio"
    "$ROOT_DIR/orchestrator/cache/huggingface"
    "$ROOT_DIR/qwen3-tts-workshop/cache/huggingface"
    "$ROOT_DIR/qwen3-tts-workshop/data/jobs"
    "$ROOT_DIR/qwen3-tts-workshop/data/outputs"
  )
  local path
  for path in "${paths[@]}"; do
    mkdir -p "$path"
  done
  verify_bind_mounts
}

verify_bind_mounts() {
  local missing=0 path
  local paths=(
    "$ROOT_DIR/media-indexer/storage"
    "$ROOT_DIR/orchestrator/data/audio"
    "$ROOT_DIR/orchestrator/cache/huggingface"
    "$ROOT_DIR/qwen3-tts-workshop/cache/huggingface"
    "$ROOT_DIR/qwen3-tts-workshop/data/references"
    "$ROOT_DIR/qwen3-tts-workshop/data/jobs"
    "$ROOT_DIR/qwen3-tts-workshop/data/outputs"
  )
  for path in "${paths[@]}"; do
    if [[ -d "$path" ]]; then
      printf 'bind   %-52s OK\n' "${path#"$ROOT_DIR/"}"
    else
      printf 'bind   %-52s MISSING\n' "${path#"$ROOT_DIR/"}" >&2
      missing=1
    fi
  done
  return "$missing"
}

ensure_network() {
  if docker network inspect "$NETWORK_NAME" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    local driver
    driver="$(docker network inspect "$NETWORK_NAME" --format '{{.Driver}}')"
    [[ "$driver" == "bridge" ]] || {
      printf 'Existing network %s uses unexpected driver %s.\n' "$NETWORK_NAME" "$driver" >&2
      return 1
    }
    return
  fi
  docker network create \
    --driver bridge \
    --label com.neovids.managed=true \
    "$NETWORK_NAME" >/dev/null
  printf 'Created shared application network: %s\n' "$NETWORK_NAME"
}

container_id() {
  compose "$1" ps --quiet "$2"
}

wait_container_health() {
  local label="$1" container="$2" timeout="$3"
  local deadline=$((SECONDS + timeout)) state
  while ((SECONDS < deadline)); do
    state="$(docker inspect --format '{{if .State.Health}}{{.State.Health.Status}}{{else}}{{.State.Status}}{{end}}' "$container" 2>/dev/null || true)"
    if [[ "$state" == "healthy" || "$state" == "running" ]]; then
      printf '%-24s READY\n' "$label"
      return
    fi
    if [[ "$state" == "unhealthy" || "$state" == "exited" || "$state" == "dead" ]]; then
      printf '%s failed with container state %s.\n' "$label" "$state" >&2
      docker logs --tail 60 "$container" >&2 || true
      return 1
    fi
    sleep 1
  done
  printf '%s did not become healthy within %ss.\n' "$label" "$timeout" >&2
  docker logs --tail 60 "$container" >&2 || true
  return 1
}

wait_http() {
  local label="$1" url="$2" timeout="$3"
  local deadline=$((SECONDS + timeout))
  while ((SECONDS < deadline)); do
    if curl --fail --silent --show-error --max-time 5 "$url" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
      printf '%-24s READY\n' "$label"
      return
    fi
    sleep 2
  done
  printf '%s did not become ready at %s within %ss.\n' "$label" "$url" "$timeout" >&2
  return 1
}

database_count() {
  local container="$1" table="$2"
  docker exec "$container" sh -ceu \
    'psql -U "$POSTGRES_USER" -d "$POSTGRES_DB" -Atc "$1"' \
    sh "select count(1) from $table"
}

verify_database_contents() {
  local ideas_db media_db orchestrator_db
  ideas_db="$(container_id ideas-hub db)"
  media_db="$(container_id media-indexer db)"
  orchestrator_db="$(container_id orchestrator db)"
  [[ -n "$ideas_db" && -n "$media_db" && -n "$orchestrator_db" ]]

  printf 'Ideas Hub ideias=%s\n' "$(database_count "$ideas_db" ideias)"
  printf 'Media Indexer sessions=%s\n' "$(database_count "$media_db" media_sessions)"
  printf 'Orchestrator workflows=%s\n' "$(database_count "$orchestrator_db" workflow_execucoes)"
}

backup_databases() {
  local destination timestamp ideas_db media_db orchestrator_db
  timestamp="$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ)"
  destination="$BACKUP_ROOT/$timestamp"
  umask 077
  mkdir -p "$destination"
  ideas_db="$(container_id ideas-hub db)"
  media_db="$(container_id media-indexer db)"
  orchestrator_db="$(container_id orchestrator db)"
  docker exec "$ideas_db" sh -ceu \
    'pg_dump -U "$POSTGRES_USER" -d "$POSTGRES_DB" -Fc' \
    >"$destination/ideas-hub.dump"
  docker exec "$media_db" sh -ceu \
    'pg_dump -U "$POSTGRES_USER" -d "$POSTGRES_DB" -Fc' \
    >"$destination/media-indexer.dump"
  docker exec "$orchestrator_db" sh -ceu \
    'pg_dump -U "$POSTGRES_USER" -d "$POSTGRES_DB" -Fc' \
    >"$destination/orchestrator.dump"
  printf 'Database backups: %s\n' "$destination"
}

migration_is_current() {
  local group="$1" service="$2" output
  if ! output="$(compose "$group" run --rm --no-deps "$service" \
    env PYTHONPATH=/app alembic current 2>&1)"; then
    printf 'Unable to inspect %s migration state:\n%s\n' "$group" "$output" >&2
    return 2
  fi
  grep -q '(head)' <<<"$output"
}

detect_pending_migrations() {
  PENDING_MIGRATIONS=()
  local status
  if migration_is_current ideas-hub backend; then
    printf 'migration %-50s CURRENT\n' "ideas-hub"
  else
    status=$?
    ((status == 1)) || return "$status"
    PENDING_MIGRATIONS+=("ideas-hub:backend")
    printf 'migration %-50s PENDING\n' "ideas-hub"
  fi
  if migration_is_current media-indexer api; then
    printf 'migration %-50s CURRENT\n' "media-indexer"
  else
    status=$?
    ((status == 1)) || return "$status"
    PENDING_MIGRATIONS+=("media-indexer:api")
    printf 'migration %-50s PENDING\n' "media-indexer"
  fi
  if migration_is_current orchestrator api; then
    printf 'migration %-50s CURRENT\n' "orchestrator"
  else
    status=$?
    ((status == 1)) || return "$status"
    PENDING_MIGRATIONS+=("orchestrator:api")
    printf 'migration %-50s PENDING\n' "orchestrator"
  fi
}

image_missing() {
  ! docker image inspect "$1" >/dev/null 2>&1
}

build_missing_images() {
  if image_missing neovids-ideas-hub-backend:local || \
    image_missing neovids-ideas-hub-frontend:local; then
    compose ideas-hub build backend frontend
  fi
  if image_missing neovids-media-indexer:local; then
    compose media-indexer build api
  fi
  if image_missing neovids-qwen-voice:local; then
    compose qwen build qwen-tts
  fi
  if image_missing neovids-video-composer:stage16; then
    compose video-composer build video-composer
  fi
  if image_missing neovids-orchestrator-backend:local || \
    image_missing neovids-orchestrator-frontend:local; then
    compose orchestrator build api frontend
  fi
}

build_all() {
  require_docker
  ensure_network
  compose ideas-hub build backend frontend
  compose media-indexer build api
  compose qwen build qwen-tts
  compose video-composer build video-composer
  compose orchestrator build api frontend
}

run_pending_migrations() {
  local entry group service
  for entry in "${PENDING_MIGRATIONS[@]}"; do
    group="${entry%%:*}"
    service="${entry##*:}"
    compose "$group" run --rm --no-deps "$service" \
      env PYTHONPATH=/app alembic upgrade head
  done
}

up_stack() {
  local option="${1:-}"
  if [[ -n "$option" && "$option" != "--build" ]]; then
    printf 'Unknown up option: %s\n' "$option" >&2
    return 2
  fi
  require_docker
  require_command curl
  prepare_installation
  ensure_network

  compose ideas-hub up --detach db
  compose media-indexer up --detach db
  compose orchestrator up --detach db redis
  wait_container_health "Ideas Hub PostgreSQL" "$(container_id ideas-hub db)" 90
  wait_container_health "Media PostgreSQL" "$(container_id media-indexer db)" 90
  wait_container_health "Orchestrator PostgreSQL" "$(container_id orchestrator db)" 90
  wait_container_health "Orchestrator Redis" "$(container_id orchestrator redis)" 60
  if [[ "$INSTALLATION_MODE" == "existing" ]]; then
    verify_database_contents
  fi

  if [[ "$option" == "--build" ]]; then
    build_all
  else
    build_missing_images
  fi

  if [[ "$INSTALLATION_MODE" == "fresh" ]]; then
    PENDING_MIGRATIONS=("ideas-hub:backend" "media-indexer:api" "orchestrator:api")
    printf 'Fresh installation: initializing database schemas without backup.\n'
  else
    detect_pending_migrations
    if ((${#PENDING_MIGRATIONS[@]})); then
      backup_databases
    else
      printf 'No pending migrations; database backup and migration steps skipped.\n'
    fi
  fi
  run_pending_migrations

  compose ideas-hub up --detach --no-build backend frontend
  wait_http "Ideas Hub API" "http://127.0.0.1:8000/health/ready" 120
  wait_http "Ideas Hub frontend" "http://127.0.0.1:5173" 120

  compose media-indexer up --detach --no-build api
  wait_http "Media Indexer" "http://127.0.0.1:8012/health/ready" 180

  compose qwen up --detach --no-build qwen-tts
  wait_http "Qwen liveness" "http://127.0.0.1:8889/health/live" 180
  wait_http "Qwen readiness" "http://127.0.0.1:8889/health/ready" 900

  compose video-composer up --detach --no-build video-composer
  wait_http "Video Composer" "http://127.0.0.1:8013/health/ready" 300

  compose orchestrator up --detach --no-build api worker frontend
  wait_http "Orchestrator API" "http://127.0.0.1:8011/health/live" 180
  wait_container_health "Orchestrator worker" "$(container_id orchestrator worker)" 180
  wait_http "Orchestrator frontend" "http://127.0.0.1:5174" 180
  wait_http "Orchestrator readiness" "http://127.0.0.1:8011/health/ready" 120

  health_stack
  status_stack
}

down_stack() {
  require_docker
  compose orchestrator down --remove-orphans
  compose video-composer down --remove-orphans
  compose qwen down --remove-orphans
  compose media-indexer down --remove-orphans
  compose ideas-hub down --remove-orphans
  printf 'NeoVids containers stopped and removed. Persistent volumes were preserved.\n'
}

status_group() {
  printf '\n[%s]\n' "$1"
  compose "$1" ps
}

status_stack() {
  local selected="${1:-}"
  if [[ -n "$selected" ]]; then
    status_group "$selected"
    return
  fi
  status_group ideas-hub
  status_group media-indexer
  status_group qwen
  status_group video-composer
  status_group orchestrator
}

check_url() {
  local label="$1" url="$2" required="${3:-true}"
  local result
  result="$(curl --silent --show-error --output /dev/null \
    --write-out '%{http_code} %{time_total}' --max-time 8 "$url" 2>/dev/null || true)"
  if [[ "$result" == 2* ]]; then
    printf '%-24s READY       %s\n' "$label" "$result"
    return
  fi
  printf '%-24s UNAVAILABLE %s\n' "$label" "${result:-connection_failed}"
  [[ "$required" != "true" ]]
}

report_port() {
  local port="$1" label="$2"
  if ss --tcp --listening --numeric "sport = :$port" | tail -n +2 | grep -q .; then
    printf 'port %-5s %-30s LISTENING\n' "$port" "$label"
  else
    printf 'port %-5s %-30s FREE\n' "$port" "$label"
  fi
}

health_stack() {
  require_command curl
  local failed=0
  check_url "LiteLLM (external)" "http://127.0.0.1:4000/health/readiness" || failed=1
  check_url "Ollama (external)" "http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/tags" false || true
  check_url "Ideas Hub" "http://127.0.0.1:8000/health/ready" || failed=1
  check_url "Media Indexer" "http://127.0.0.1:8012/health/ready" || failed=1
  check_url "Qwen Voice" "http://127.0.0.1:8889/health/ready" || failed=1
  check_url "Video Composer" "http://127.0.0.1:8013/health/ready" || failed=1
  check_url "Orchestrator" "http://127.0.0.1:8011/health/ready" || failed=1
  check_url "Ideas Hub frontend" "http://127.0.0.1:5173" || failed=1
  check_url "Orchestrator frontend" "http://127.0.0.1:5174" || failed=1
  return "$failed"
}

doctor() {
  local failed=0 current=0 group count
  printf 'NeoVids doctor (read-only)\n'
  require_docker || failed=1
  if ((failed)); then
    return "$failed"
  fi
  detect_installation_mode
  case "$INSTALLATION_MODE" in
    existing)
      printf 'installation %-47s EXISTING\n' "NeoVids durable state"
      verify_volume_identity || failed=1
      verify_bind_mounts || failed=1
      ;;
    fresh)
      printf 'installation %-47s FRESH (bootstrapped by up)\n' "NeoVids durable state"
      ;;
    partial)
      printf 'installation %-47s PARTIAL / AMBIGUOUS\n' "NeoVids durable state" >&2
      verify_volume_identity || true
      failed=1
      ;;
  esac
  if docker network inspect "$NETWORK_NAME" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    printf 'network %-51s PRESENT\n' "$NETWORK_NAME"
  else
    printf 'network %-51s ABSENT (created by up)\n' "$NETWORK_NAME"
  fi
  printf '\nDisk:\n'
  df -h "$ROOT_DIR" | tail -n 1
  printf '\nMemory:\n'
  free -h | sed -n '1,3p'
  printf '\nGPU:\n'
  if command -v nvidia-smi >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    nvidia-smi --query-gpu=name,memory.total,memory.used,utilization.gpu \
      --format=csv,noheader,nounits || failed=1
  else
    printf 'nvidia-smi unavailable\n'
    failed=1
  fi
  printf '\nExternal dependencies:\n'
  check_url "LiteLLM" "http://127.0.0.1:4000/health/readiness" || failed=1
  check_url "Ollama" "http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/tags" false || true
  printf '\nHost ports:\n'
  report_port 8000 "Ideas Hub API"
  report_port 5173 "Ideas Hub frontend"
  report_port 5432 "Ideas Hub PostgreSQL"
  report_port 8012 "Media Indexer API"
  report_port 5435 "Media Indexer PostgreSQL"
  report_port 8889 "Qwen Voice"
  report_port 8013 "Video Composer"
  report_port 8011 "Orchestrator API"
  report_port 5174 "Orchestrator frontend"
  report_port 5434 "Orchestrator PostgreSQL"
  report_port 6380 "Orchestrator Redis"
  printf '\nApplication endpoints (informational before up):\n'
  check_url "Ideas Hub" "http://127.0.0.1:8000/health/live" false || true
  check_url "Media Indexer" "http://127.0.0.1:8012/health/live" false || true
  check_url "Qwen Voice" "http://127.0.0.1:8889/health/live" false || true
  check_url "Video Composer" "http://127.0.0.1:8013/health/live" false || true
  check_url "Orchestrator" "http://127.0.0.1:8011/health/live" false || true
  for group in ideas-hub media-indexer orchestrator qwen3-tts-workshop video-composer; do
    count="$(docker ps --all --filter "label=com.docker.compose.project=$group" --quiet | wc -l)"
    current=$((current + count))
  done
  printf '\nNeoVids containers currently present: %s\n' "$current"
  return "$failed"
}

logs_group() {
  compose "$1" logs --tail 200
}

logs_stack() {
  local selected="${1:-}"
  if [[ -n "$selected" ]]; then
    logs_group "$selected"
    return
  fi
  logs_group ideas-hub
  logs_group media-indexer
  logs_group qwen
  logs_group video-composer
  logs_group orchestrator
}

restart_group() {
  case "$1" in
    ideas-hub)
      compose ideas-hub restart backend frontend
      wait_http "Ideas Hub API" "http://127.0.0.1:8000/health/ready" 120
      wait_http "Ideas Hub frontend" "http://127.0.0.1:5173" 120
      ;;
    media-indexer)
      compose media-indexer restart api
      wait_http "Media Indexer" "http://127.0.0.1:8012/health/ready" 180
      ;;
    qwen)
      compose qwen restart qwen-tts
      wait_http "Qwen liveness" "http://127.0.0.1:8889/health/live" 180
      wait_http "Qwen readiness" "http://127.0.0.1:8889/health/ready" 900
      ;;
    video-composer)
      compose video-composer restart video-composer
      wait_http "Video Composer" "http://127.0.0.1:8013/health/ready" 300
      ;;
    orchestrator)
      compose orchestrator restart api worker frontend
      wait_http "Orchestrator API" "http://127.0.0.1:8011/health/live" 180
      wait_container_health "Orchestrator worker" "$(container_id orchestrator worker)" 180
      wait_http "Orchestrator frontend" "http://127.0.0.1:5174" 180
      wait_http "Orchestrator readiness" "http://127.0.0.1:8011/health/ready" 120
      ;;
    *) printf 'Unknown service group: %s\n' "$1" >&2; return 2 ;;
  esac
}

main() {
  local command="${1:-}"
  case "$command" in
    doctor) doctor ;;
    up)
      [[ $# -le 2 ]] || { usage >&2; return 2; }
      up_stack "${2:-}"
      ;;
    down) down_stack ;;
    restart)
      if [[ -n "${2:-}" ]]; then restart_group "$2"; else down_stack; up_stack; fi
      ;;
    status) status_stack "${2:-}" ;;
    health) health_stack ;;
    logs) logs_stack "${2:-}" ;;
    build) build_all ;;
    -h|--help|help|"") usage ;;
    *) usage >&2; return 2 ;;
  esac
}

if [[ "${NEOVIDS_LIB_ONLY:-0}" != "1" ]]; then
  main "$@"
fi
</file>

<file path="README.md">
# NeoVids infrastructure

Version-controlled operational layer for the five NeoVids service repositories.
It owns only cross-service Docker orchestration, the root operational CLI,
Compose overrides and operational documentation.

See [`infra/README.md`](infra/README.md) for architecture, storage contracts,
commands and troubleshooting.

For a clean Ubuntu 24.04 installation, GPU/Docker setup, repository cloning,
configuration, smoke tests and daily operations, follow the
[`INSTALLATION_GUIDE.md`](INSTALLATION_GUIDE.md).

From the parent NeoVids workspace, the compatibility symlinks preserve the
normal workflow:

```bash
./scripts/neovids doctor
./scripts/neovids up
./scripts/neovids health
./scripts/neovids down
```

They are optional because `./neovids-infra/scripts/neovids` works directly. To
recreate the convenient paths in a workspace where they do not exist, run from
the parent directory:

```bash
ln -s neovids-infra/scripts scripts
ln -s neovids-infra/infra infra
```
